  "rule": "Objects on a background-7 grid are sorted by cell count, largest first; the output is a (2n-1)-square of concentric rings coloured from the outer frame (largest object) to the centre cell (smallest object).",
  "scope": "Supports 2..6 single-colour 4-connected polyomino objects (1..12 cells) with pairwise distinct sizes and distinct non-7 colours, separated so no two touch even diagonally, on 6..16 input grids. Background fixed at 7 (intrinsic). Not supported: equal-size objects (ambiguous order), objects touching each other, multicolour objects, non-7 backgrounds, more than 6 objects.",
  "constraints": [
    "All object cell counts are pairwise distinct so the size ordering is unambiguous.",
    "All object colours are distinct and differ from background 7.",
    "Objects are placed with a one-cell buffer so that 8-connected component extraction recovers exactly the latent objects.",
    "Each object is a single 4-connected (hence 8-connected) polyomino.",
    "Output side is 2n-1 and is never equal to the input, so no example is identity."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
